boethius-2.md:1: argue/answered: S3: answered no, which keeps boethius-2.logic.r1, to: Suppose "offices of state have power to plant virtue in the minds of their possessors and drive out vice", "offices of state are rather wont to signalize iniquity than to chase it away" and "honours so often fall to the most iniquitous of men" are true. Is S3, "Nay, they are rather wont to signalize iniquity than to chase it away, and hence arises our indignation that honours so often fall to the most iniquitous of men.", true then? [in 1 of 2 runs]
